    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes and the idempotency acceptance test is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation keyed on the `Idempotency-Key` header, so a repeated create with an already-seen key returns the originally created owner with `200` instead of creating a duplicate (which would otherwise 409 on the household-duplicate check).\n\nChanges, each kept in its proper place:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `Idempotency-Key` header parameter and a `200` response to the `addOwner` operation. Regenerating the API gives the controller interface a `@RequestHeader(value = \"Idempotency-Key\", required = false) String idempotencyKey` parameter, so the header is read the conventional, spec-driven way rather than pulled from the raw request.\n\n2. **`service/OwnerCreationIdempotencyStore.java`** (new) \u2014 A small single-responsibility component that remembers which owner id was created for each key (thread-safe `ConcurrentHashMap`, first-write-wins via `putIfAbsent`). It mirrors the existing `OwnerAuditLogger` pattern of an injected owner-lifecycle support bean.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Injected the store, updated `addOwner` to the new signature, and:\n   - Before any validation/creation, a private `replayIdempotentCreate` helper returns the original owner (mapped to a DTO with `200`) when the key has already produced a still-existing owner.\n   - After a successful save, records the key \u2192 new owner id.\n\nThe controller's existing validation and creation logic is untouched; the new behavior is a thin guard at the front and one record call at the end, delegating storage to the dedicated component. Full suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
