    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`. The handler is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(...)` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:176-230`).\n\n## Phase A \u2014 Gate & framework validation (before the method body runs)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (line 174). Caller must hold `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`. *(Enforced only when `petclinic.security.enable=true`; otherwise `DisableSecurityConfig` permits all.)*\n\n2. **Bean Validation on the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`** \u2014 fails \u2192 400. Constraints:\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max=10)`\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max=255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max=255)`\n   - `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid`\n\n## Phase B \u2014 Controller method body (exact order)\n\n3. **Idempotency replay** (177-180) \u2014 if the `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before, load the previously-created owner and **return 200** immediately (short-circuits everything below; no new create).\n4. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** (182), via MapStruct (`sharesHousehold` handled separately later).\n5. **Address normalization + required check** (183-185) \u2014 trim/collapse/upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET etc.; structured `addressLine1` overrides flat `address`. Neither present \u2192 400.\n6. **Telephone \u2192 E.164** (186-190) \u2014 normalize; assumes country code 61 if no `+CC`; must be 8\u201315 digits. Empty result \u2192 400.\n7. **Email normalization + validity + disposable-domain check** (191-194) \u2014 lower-case/trim; invalid format or disposable domain (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail) \u2192 400.\n8. **Postcode validity** (195-197) \u2014 if present, must be 4 digits and within the city's region range \u2192 else 400.\n9. **Future registration-date rejection** (198-201) \u2014 supplied date after today \u2192 400.\n10. **Registration-date defaulting + business-day roll-forward** (202-204) \u2014 default to today if null; roll weekends/holidays forward.\n11. **Per-day cap** (205-207) \u2014 `countOwnersByRegistrationDate >= 100` \u2192 **429**.\n12. **Apply normalized telephone + email onto entity** (208-209).\n13. **Per-city cap** (210-212) \u2014 `countOwnersByCity >= 50` \u2192 **409**.\n14. **Household-duplicate check** (213-219) \u2014 if `sharesHousehold` not declared and `isHouseholdOccupied` (last name + postcode) \u2192 **409**.\n15. **Set transient declared-household-member flag** (220).\n16. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (221) \u2014 see Phase C.\n17. **Audit log side-effect** (222) \u2014 `ownerAuditLogger.logCreated(owner)` writes an `AUDIT` INFO line.\n18. **Remember idempotency key** (223-225) \u2014 store `key \u2192 owner.id` (first write wins).\n19. **Build 201 response** (226-229) \u2014 map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Phase C \u2014 Service side-effects inside `saveOwner` (`ClinicServiceImpl.java:250-271`, `@Transactional`)\n\nFor a new owner, these derived fields are stamped **before** the repository save:\n\n20. **customerCode** \u2014 generated `<REGION>-<HASH8>` if null (collision-checked, unique).\n21. **namesakeCount** \u2014 count of existing owners with same first+last name.\n22. **bulkSignupWarning** \u2014 set true if day's registrations `> 80`.\n23. **householdId** \u2014 SHA-256(lastName|postcode) prefix; null if no postcode.\n24. **householdSize** \u2014 count in household + 1 (else 1).\n25. **possibleDuplicate / possibleDuplicateOf** \u2014 flag an existing same-household owner with a different phone.\n26. **`ownerRepository.save(owner)`** \u2014 `persist` (new).\n\n## Phase D \u2014 Persistence flush (last, inside the transaction)\n\n27. **`@PrePersist Owner.normalizeRegistrationDate()`** (`Owner.java:454-460`) \u2014 re-defaults/rolls-forward registration date on flush.\n28. **Entity-level Bean Validation at flush** \u2014 `Owner.address`/`city`/`firstName`/`lastName` `@NotEmpty`; `Owner.telephone` `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)`; `deleted` non-null.\n\n**Terminal outcomes:** 200 (idempotent replay), 201 (created), 400 (address/phone/email/postcode/future-date/DTO), 409 (city cap or household duplicate), 429 (daily cap), 401/403 (auth). Exception mapping is in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the caps at steps 11/13 and the household check at 14 are plain read-then-write checks with no locking, so they're racy under concurrency \u2014 but you asked only for what's applied, and that's the full ordered list."
